## Box Model of HTML

The **Box Model** is a concept in CSS that describes how every HTML element is represented as a rectangular box.

The CSS Box Model consists of four parts:

1. **Content** – The actual text or content of the element.
2. **Padding** – The space between the content and the border.
3. **Border** – The boundary around the padding and content.
4. **Margin** – The space outside the border.

### Box Model Structure

```text
        ┌─────────────────────────────┐
        │           Margin            │
        │   ┌─────────────────────┐   │
        │   │       Border        │   │
        │   │  ┌───────────────┐  │   │
        │   │  │    Padding    │  │   │
        │   │  │ ┌───────────┐ │  │   │
        │   │  │ │  Content  │ │  │   │
        │   │  │ └───────────┘ │  │   │
        │   │  └───────────────┘  │   │
        │   └─────────────────────┘   │
        └─────────────────────────────┘
```

Thus, the box model can be represented as:

**Content → Padding → Border → Margin
## HTML and CSS Program

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>CSS Box Model</title>

    <style>
        .welcome {
            margin: 20px;
            padding: 10px;
            color: white;
            background-color: black;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <p class="welcome">Welcome to IGNOU</p>

</body>
</html>
### Explanation

* `margin: 20px;` → Provides **20px space on all four sides** of the element.
* `padding: 10px;` → Provides **10px space between the text and its boundary**.
* `color: white;` → Makes the text **white**.
* `background-color: black;` → Sets the background color to **black**.
* `class="welcome"` → Connects the HTML paragraph with the CSS rules.

### Output

The text **"Welcome to IGNOU"** will appear with:

* **20px margin** on all sides
* **10px padding** on all sides
* **White text**
* **Black background**
