Q8. Explain the uses of any five HTML
elements which are used in form design.

## HTML Elements Used in Form Design

HTML provides various elements for creating forms. A form is used to collect information from users, such as name, email, password, address, etc.

### 1. `<form>` Element

* The `<form>` element is used to create an HTML form.
* It acts as a container for all form controls.
* It specifies where and how the form data will be submitted.

**Example:**

```html
<form action="submit.php" method="post">
    ...
</form>
```

### 2. `<input>` Element

* The `<input>` element is used to create different types of input fields.
* It can be used for text, password, email, radio buttons, checkboxes, etc.

**Example:**

```html
<input type="text" name="username">
<input type="password" name="password">
```

### 3. `<textarea>` Element

* The `<textarea>` element is used to enter **multiple lines of text**.
* It is commonly used for comments, feedback, and addresses.

**Example:**

```html
<textarea name="address" rows="4" cols="30"></textarea>
```

### 4. `<select>` Element

* The `<select>` element creates a **drop-down list**.
* It allows the user to select one option from a list.

**Example:**

```html
<select name="course">
    <option>BCA</option>
    <option>MCA</option>
    <option>BBA</option>
</select>
```

### 5. `<button>` Element

* The `<button>` element is used to create a clickable button.
* It can be used for submitting a form or performing other actions.

**Example:**

```html
<button type="submit">Submit</button>
```----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------